      "textEn": "63\n(free), kamini (lustful) and pumschali (seductive by men). From Atal,\nbelow is the planet Vittal, where Lord Shiva resides with his wife Gauri. From their presence,\na type of gold is produced, which is called Hatak. Below Vitthal, in the Sutal planet, is the abode of the supremely fortunate Bali Maharaj. Lord Vamandev, pleased with their difficult penance,\nshowed mercy on Bali Maharaj. They went with him to the place of sacrifice and, on the same pretext, after asking for three steps of land,\ntook all their property. Upon Bali Maharaj being ready to give everything, the Lord became very pleased.\nAs a result, he became their gatekeeper. The description of Bali Maharaj is in the eighth\nchapter of Shrimad Bhagwat. When God grants material pleasures to a devotee, it is not their true blessing.\nIt is not. The gods, inflamed by the pride of their splendor, pray to God only for material pleasures. But devotees like Prahlad Maharaj do not desire material pleasures.\nWhat is the point of material happiness, they\ndo not desire liberation from material bondage, although liberation can be attained even by chanting with impure utterances of the holy name. Below Tālatala is the Talatala, which is the abode of the demon Maya. By the blessings of Lord Shankar, this\ndemon is extremely happy in terms of material sight, but he never attains spiritual happiness. Below the bottom\nThere is also a great realm below where there are many snakes with hundreds and thousands of hoods. Below the great lake is Rasatal, and\nEven below that is Patal Lok, where Nag Vasuki resides with his companions.\nSreesukha said,\n\nAdhastasvituryayojaneyujate swarbhanu nakshatravacharatyetyeko yosahavamaratvam grahatvam chalabhat bhagavadanukampaya\nSwayamasurapasadaha sainikeyo hyatadarhasthasya tata janma karmani choparishtadvakshyamah. 1. Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Shuka said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami spoke; Adhastat—below; Savitu—Sun's sphere; Yojana—equal to eight miles; Ayut