      "textEn": "68\n\nAnd it will be affected by the arrival of disease. Without caring about the next birth, completely materialistic,\nthey want to be engrossed in enjoying pleasure in their short life. To such deluded materialists,\nVaishnavas are always eager to provide the real pleasure of spiritual bliss. Yeshu Maharaj, these are the structures built without illusion.\n\nWith the entrance of the best of jeweled gems, the strange building complex, the assembly hall, the four-storied temple, and other such things, adorned with the lotus-like eyes of the serpent-king, the one who is the abode of the gods. 9. Meaning of the word\n\nYeshu—in those lower worlds; Maha-raj—O King; Mayen—by the demon Maya; Maya-vina—skilled in architecture; Vinirmitah—\nmade; Purah—cities; Nana-mani-pravara—of precious gems; Pravek—the best; Virachit—made; Vichitra—\nwonderful; Bhavan—house; Prakar—walls; Gopur—gate; Sabha—assembly hall; Chaitya—temple; Chatvara—schools; Ayatan—\netc.—Including hotels or entertainment halls, etc.; Nag—animals with a body like a serpent; Asura—demons or\nOf the non-believing people; by the twos; by the pairs; by the doves; by the parrots; by the mynas; by the parrots; by the groups;\nArtificial—made-up; from the earth—from the ground; by the lord of the worlds—by the lords of the worlds; by the best houses—by the best houses; by the decorated—adorned; by the shining—shining;\nDecorated—adorned; by the chakras—by the sparkles. Hey Rajan, in artificial heaven, which is called Bill-Swarg, there is a great demon named Maya who\nis an extremely skilled architect. He has constructed many ornate cities where many\nstrange buildings, ramparts, gates, assembly halls, temples, courtyards, and the residence of foreigners\nhave hotels and residences. The buildings of the rulers of these planets have been made with extremely valuable gems. These buildings are full of many pigeons, parrots, and other\nbirds, in addition to snakes and demons. Overall, these artificial heavenly cities are very attractively\ndecorated.\n"
