      "textEn": "78\n\nAnd the creature progresses towards the state of pure chanting. In the third stage, when a being, free from sin,\nchants the Hare Krishna mantra, his latent love for Krishna immediately awakens. It is the ultimate achievement. Of those who are devoted, for all of them, the Self is the Self, and the Self is the Self. 21. Meaning of the word\n\nThat—that; of the devotees—of the devotees; of the self-realized men like Sanaka and Sanatana; of all—of all;\nOf the self—up to the self-formed Shri Bhagavan; of the self-giver—who gives himself without hesitation; of the self—that supreme self\nis, the Supreme Soul; Ev—indeed. In the heart of every creature, the hands of devotees like Shri Bhagwan Narad Muni, who are situated as the form of God,\nget sold. In other words, God loves such devotees and those who love him with pure\nfeelings. They surrender themselves to his hands. Even the great self-\nrealizing yogis, like the four princes, also attain divine bliss by realizing the Supreme Being within themselves.\nMeaning: Shri Bhagwan Bali Maharaj was not made the doorkeeper because he had dedicated his everything, but because he had attained high position and success as a lover. Not by the Lord, but by the self-realized, who, when they are born, do not forget their own self, but shatter the illusionary pleasures. 22. Meaning of the word\n\nN—No; Va—Indeed; Bhagavan—Lord; Noonam—Certainly; Amushya—To Bali Maharaj; Anujagraha—Showed one's grace; Yat—Because; Ut—Indeed; Punah—Again; Atma-anumasiti—Remembering Shri Bhagavan; Moshanam—One who steals;\nMaya-Maya—A quality of Maya; Bhog-Aishwaryam—Material opulence; Ev—Indeed; Atanut—Forgetful; Iti—Thus..\n\nShri Bhagwan did not show his grace by granting material happiness and opulence to Bali Maharaj because it makes one forget God's love and devotion. The result of material opulence\nis that one no longer feels inclined towards God.\nMeaning: There are two types of opulence—one that is born of actions and 