      "textEn": "81\n\nYesyanudasya mevatpitamahah kil vavre na tu swapitryam yadutakutabhayam padam deyamanam bhagavatan para miti\nBhagavatoparate khalu swapitarri. 2. Meaning of the word\n\nYasya—Of whom (Shri Bhagavan); Anudasyaam—Served; Eva—Certainly; Asmat—Ours; Pitamahah—Paternal grandfather, Baba;\nKil—Undoubtedly; Vavre—Accepted; Na—Not; Tu—But; Swa—Own; Pitryam—Paternal property; Yat—That; Ut—Certainly;\nAkutam—Fear; Padam—Post; Diyamanam—When given; Bhagavatam—By God; Param—Other; Iti—Thus; Bhagavatam—By Shri Bhagavan; Uparate—When killed; Khal—Undoubtedly; Swa-Pitarim—Own father. Bali Maharaj said—My great-grandfather Prahlad Maharaj was the only such person who\nrecognized self-interest. After the death of his father Hiranyakashipu, Lord Narasimhadeva wanted to grant Prahlad\nhis father's empire along with freedom from material bonds, but Prahlad did not accept any of them.\nHe thought that liberation and\nmaterial opulence are obstacles in devotion, therefore, to obtain such a boon from Shri Bhagwan is not\nthe real grace of God. As a result, Prahlad, not accepting the fruits of action and knowledge,\nMaharaj asked for a boon from God to remain absorbed in the devotion of his servant. Meaning: Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu's teaching is that a pure devotee considers himself as a servant of God's servant.\n(Gopibhartuha Padamalayor Dasadasanudasah)). In Vaishnava philosophy, no one should become a direct servant.\nShould not. Prahlad Maharaj had been blessed with a glorious position in this world and the freedom to be one with Brahma, but he rejected them. He considered it better to remain engaged in the service of even the servants of God. Therefore, Bali Maharaj has said that because his great-grandfather Prahlad\nMaharaj had denied the blessings of Shri Bhagwan, such as material opulence and freedom from bondage,\ntherefore, he understood self-interest very well.\nBy whose greatness, by whose unparalleled merit, by whose austerity, by whose devotion, is one who has not attained liberation, approached by the grace of the Lord. 26. Meaning of the word.\n\nOf him—of Prahlad Maharaj; Maha-anubhutasya—who was a great devotee; Anupatham—path; Amrjit-kashayah—stained by materialism;\nMan; Who?; Or; As to us—like us; Parihin-Bhagavat-anugraha—without the grace of Shri Bhagavan;\nUpajigamishati—wants to follow; Thus—in this way. Bali Maharaj said—Men like us, who are still engrossed in material pleasures, who\nare tainted by the three qualities of material nature and who lack the grace of Shri Bhagwan, they"
